WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:05.820
Your goal is simple: eliminate all disease. The constraint is also simple: resources are scarce.

2
00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:13.400
You have limited money, time, and talent. Every dollar on a low-impact trial is a dollar not curing cancer.

3
00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:18.620
Every researcher writing grant applications is a researcher not doing research.

4
00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:24.940
Every patient excluded from trials is data you'll never collect and a person you'll never help.

5
00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:30.990
Your current system fails this optimization so thoroughly it almost looks intentional.

6
00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:38.660
Your N.I.H. spends forty-seven billion dollars a year. Your scientists spend fifty to sixty-seven percent of their time

7
00:00:38.660 --> 00:00:45.600
writing grant applications instead of doing science. Billions flow to projects that never produce treatments.

8
00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:51.650
Your system isn't designed to maximize cures. It's designed to maximize grant-writing.

9
00:00:52.580 --> 00:00:58.740
This isn't a conspiracy. It's just what happens when you design a system that rewards asking for money instead of producing

10
00:00:58.740 --> 00:01:07.100
results. You've accidentally built a machine whose primary output is paperwork and whose secondary output is occasionally,

11
00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:15.380
reluctantly, medicine. Your Decentralized Institute of Health, or D.I.H., is an alternative design that optimizes for a

12
00:01:15.380 --> 00:01:23.180
single metric: maximum ROI toward disease eradication. It's what you'd build if you started from scratch and actually wanted

13
00:01:23.180 --> 00:01:28.320
results. The Health-Industrial Complex: Coordinating Your War on Disease.

14
00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:37.180
The Olsonian Problem. Your economist Mancur Olson identified why public goods are systematically underproduced: diffuse

15
00:01:37.180 --> 00:01:45.000
benefits and concentrated costs. In simpler terms: everyone benefits from a cure for cancer, but nobody benefits enough

16
00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:49.120
to fight for it the way a weapons manufacturer fights for a bomber contract.

17
00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:57.600
It's one of those observations that's obvious once someone says it, and invisible before, which describes most of your species'

18
00:01:57.760 --> 00:02:01.880
problems. Curing cancer benefits eight billion people a little.

19
00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:07.340
Blocking cancer cures benefits a few thousand pharmaceutical executives a lot.

20
00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:15.740
The executives show up to lobby. The eight billion don't. This is why your species has spent fifty years "fighting cancer"

21
00:02:16.120 --> 00:02:20.820
while your defense industry got stealth bombers, aircraft carriers, and G.P.S.

22
00:02:21.520 --> 00:02:25.260
Your military-industrial complex solved this problem for defense.

23
00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:32.680
Defense contractors, generals, politicians, and workers all have concentrated interests in military spending.

24
00:02:33.320 --> 00:02:39.580
They coordinate. They lobby. They win budgets. Result: the most powerful military in human history.

25
00:02:40.600 --> 00:02:44.940
Disease has no such coalition. Your patients are too sick to lobby.

26
00:02:45.340 --> 00:02:49.840
Your researchers compete for scraps. Your funders lack coordination.

27
00:02:50.240 --> 00:02:56.740
Your politicians get no credit for cures that arrive after their term ends (which is all of them, because cures take fifteen

28
00:02:56.740 --> 00:03:04.820
years and terms last four). Everyone wants disease eradicated; no one has a concentrated interest in making it happen.

29
00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:12.320
It's like everyone wanting a clean kitchen but nobody wanting to do the dishes, except the dishes are cancer and the kitchen

30
00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:19.920
is on fire. Your D.I.H. solves the Olsonian problem by creating concentrated interests in disease eradication.

31
00:03:20.740 --> 00:03:25.380
Your military-industrial complex coordinates actors around defense.

32
00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:35.330
Your decentralized institutes of health, or D.I.H., creates a HEALTH-INDUSTRIAL COMPLEX that coordinates actors around eradication.

33
00:03:35.780 --> 00:03:46.660
Same structure, opposite purpose. Supreme Headquarters Allied Expeditionary Force, or SHAEF, for Your War on Disease.

34
00:03:47.320 --> 00:03:51.400
In nineteen forty-four, Eisenhower didn't replace the Allied armies.

35
00:03:51.680 --> 00:03:58.840
He coordinated them. Set the objective, allocated resources, made sure everyone pulled in the same direction.

36
00:03:59.560 --> 00:04:06.480
YOUR D.I.H. IS SHAEF FOR THE WAR ON DISEASE. Pharma companies stay pharma companies.

37
00:04:07.300 --> 00:04:11.560
Universities stay universities. Patient groups stay patient groups.

38
00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:18.380
But they operate as one force because your D.I.H. coordinates them toward eradication.

39
00:04:18.959 --> 00:04:24.200
Your war on disease has been losing for fifty years because it's not actually a war.

40
00:04:24.560 --> 00:04:32.000
It's a collection of uncoordinated skirmishes where researchers compete for grants, pharma companies hide failures, and

41
00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:41.900
patients can't access trials. You've been "fighting" cancer the way a cat "fights" a laser pointer: lots of energy, no coordination,

42
00:04:42.280 --> 00:04:49.300
nothing caught. Imagine if D-Day had been run this way. The Americans land at one beach, the British at another.

43
00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:56.380
Neither tells the other what they learned. Both compete for the same supply ships while the enemy reads their grant applications.

44
00:04:57.140 --> 00:05:03.930
Your D.I.H. is the coordination layer that turns scattered skirmishes into a unified campaign.

45
00:05:04.180 --> 00:05:10.900
Your D.I.H.: The return on investment, or R.O.I., Maximization Protocol.

46
00:05:11.720 --> 00:05:16.800
Your D.I.H. is not a platform. It's not an organization. It's not even really a thing.

47
00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:24.400
It's a COORDINATION PROTOCOL with one function: MAKE EVERY ACTOR DO THE HIGHEST-R.O.I.

48
00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:31.200
THING TOWARD TOTAL DISEASE ERADICATION. This means: Every dollar flows to maximum impact.

49
00:05:31.780 --> 00:05:38.900
Every researcher works on highest-value problems. Every patient joins trials that matter most.

50
00:05:39.120 --> 00:05:45.060
Nothing gets wasted on low-R.O.I. activities. On your planet, you call this radical.

51
00:05:45.660 --> 00:05:54.860
On mine, we call it "obvious." Three Core Functions. One. RECEIVE FUNDS (from the one percent Treaty, donations, etc.).

52
00:05:55.400 --> 00:06:03.100
Two. ALLOCATE RESEARCH VIA PATIENT SUBSIDIES (market mechanism) and INFRASTRUCTURE VIA Wishocracy.

53
00:06:03.340 --> 00:06:10.710
Three. VERIFY RESULTS AND PAY PROPORTIONAL TO IMPACT. Everything operational is outsourced.

54
00:06:10.920 --> 00:06:14.540
Trial infrastructure? That's your decentralized F.D.A.'s job.

55
00:06:15.400 --> 00:06:20.560
Task decomposition? A.I. services. Talent matching? Existing marketplaces.

56
00:06:21.040 --> 00:06:28.800
Crowdfunding? Existing platforms. Why stay thin? Because THIN PROTOCOLS ARE HARD TO CAPTURE.

57
00:06:28.800 --> 00:06:32.680
There's nothing to bribe. No operational role to corrupt. No C.E.O.

58
00:06:32.880 --> 00:06:38.100
to take on a yacht trip. Just code that moves money toward measured outcomes.

59
00:06:38.980 --> 00:06:42.840
Your species has a habit of corrupting every institution you build.

60
00:06:43.360 --> 00:06:48.780
You corrupt them the way water corrodes pipes: inevitably, given enough time and contact.

61
00:06:49.440 --> 00:06:55.560
This one is boring enough that nobody bothers. The Core Innovation: Pay for Results.

62
00:06:56.300 --> 00:07:03.680
Every dollar flows based on results, not promises: Patients vote with their enrollment, meaning researchers get paid for

63
00:07:03.680 --> 00:07:11.120
attracting patients. Outcomes determine continued funding, meaning campaigns that deliver get more; failures get defunded.

64
00:07:11.920 --> 00:07:15.980
No one gets paid for writing grant proposals. No one gets paid for attending review committees.

65
00:07:16.980 --> 00:07:20.880
No one gets paid for publishing papers about why their research might work someday.

66
00:07:21.700 --> 00:07:27.610
This is how most other industries work. You pay contractors when they build the house, not when they promise to build it.

67
00:07:27.960 --> 00:07:31.540
You pay farmers when they grow the food, not when they apply for a farming license.

68
00:07:33.080 --> 00:07:38.420
Your Data Commons: Publish Everything. Your current system hides failures.

69
00:07:39.120 --> 00:07:43.200
Companies bury negative results. Researchers don't publish what didn't work.

70
00:07:43.840 --> 00:07:50.720
Your scientists waste billions repeating mistakes someone else already made because they literally cannot find out those

71
00:07:50.720 --> 00:07:56.320
mistakes were already made. It's like your whole species has amnesia, but only for the embarrassing parts.

72
00:07:57.060 --> 00:08:01.390
You remember your triumphs in high definition and forget your failures completely.

73
00:08:01.480 --> 00:08:04.400
This is called "being human." It's also called "why you keep dying.".

74
00:08:05.680 --> 00:08:14.080
Your D.I.H. requires ONE HUNDRED PERCENT OPEN PUBLICATION of all data, positive and negative, as a condition of funding:

75
00:08:14.220 --> 00:08:18.760
Every trial, every result, and every dataset is published. A.I.

76
00:08:18.920 --> 00:08:22.520
models scan the global data commons, finding patterns humans miss.

77
00:08:23.240 --> 00:08:26.280
Failed experiments become shared knowledge, not repeated waste.

78
00:08:27.040 --> 00:08:32.280
This is intelligence sharing in the Supreme Headquarters Allied Expeditionary Force, or S.H.A.E.F., analogy.

79
00:08:33.020 --> 00:08:36.820
Your Allies won partly because they shared Ultra intercepts across commands.

80
00:08:37.559 --> 00:08:42.220
Your war on disease loses because everyone guards their failures like trade secrets.

81
00:08:42.880 --> 00:08:45.520
Think of it as a group chat where everyone shares what didn't work.

82
00:08:46.240 --> 00:08:50.420
Except the group is your entire species and the topic is death prevention.

83
00:08:51.320 --> 00:08:59.600
Governance: Market Mechanism plus Wishocracy. Your D.I.H. uses two allocation mechanisms: Patient subsidies (market mechanism):

84
00:09:00.820 --> 00:09:06.220
Research funding follows patient choice. Patients enroll in trials they believe in; funding flows accordingly.

85
00:09:07.060 --> 00:09:13.480
Variable subsidy rates ensure rare diseases remain viable. No committees decide "cancer versus Alzheimer's.".

86
00:09:14.440 --> 00:09:21.620
Wishocracy: For infrastructure and public goods only. It aggregates preferences through pairwise comparisons (electronic

87
00:09:21.620 --> 00:09:23.600
health record, or E.H.R., integration or security audits?).

88
00:09:24.920 --> 00:09:30.200
The Incentive Stack: Making R.O.I. the Selfish Choice. Your D.I.H.

89
00:09:30.200 --> 00:09:37.540
doesn't rely on altruism. Altruism is lovely but flaky. It shows up when it feels like it, cancels last minute, and is always

90
00:09:37.540 --> 00:09:42.790
"busy that weekend." Instead, your D.I.H. PAYS EVERYONE to do the highest-R.O.I.

91
00:09:43.160 --> 00:09:48.720
thing. Greed is more dependable than kindness. Your entire economic system proves this daily.

92
00:09:49.720 --> 00:09:55.620
Nobody ever forgot to be greedy. Researchers are driven by money and prestige; the D.I.H.

93
00:09:55.620 --> 00:10:02.600
provides per-patient subsidies that are higher for rare diseases, ensuring that attracting patients gets them paid.

94
00:10:03.660 --> 00:10:11.860
Patients are driven by health and compensation; the D.I.H. provides subsidies that scale with trial importance, ensuring

95
00:10:11.860 --> 00:10:21.200
that joining high-priority trials results in more pay. Politicians are driven by re-election and legacy; the D.I.H.

96
00:10:21.200 --> 00:10:30.100
provides incentive-alignment bonds, or I.A.B.s, tied to disease outcomes, ensuring better outcomes lead to a bigger bonus.

97
00:10:31.440 --> 00:10:41.240
Funders are driven by impact and returns; the D.I.H. provides quadratic matching and outcome tracking, ensuring high-R.O.I.

98
00:10:41.240 --> 00:10:47.960
donations have an amplified impact. Data providers are driven by revenue; the D.I.H.

99
00:10:47.960 --> 00:10:54.400
provides fees tied to data utility, ensuring more useful data results in more revenue.

100
00:10:55.380 --> 00:11:04.340
Campaigns are driven by funding; the D.I.H. provides results-based continued funding, ensuring a higher R.O.I.

101
00:11:04.420 --> 00:11:14.560
leads to more funding. Every incentive is R.O.I.-weighted. Not just "do good" but "do the MOST good per dollar per hour."

102
00:11:15.360 --> 00:11:22.000
Your D.I.H. makes the highest-R.O.I. action the selfish choice for every actor.

103
00:11:22.920 --> 00:11:29.000
Selfishness, properly directed, cures cancer. How Your Researchers Get Paid.

104
00:11:29.340 --> 00:11:33.940
Your traditional system: Write a grant proposal. Hope a committee likes it.

105
00:11:34.500 --> 00:11:39.460
Get paid to try. Maybe produce results. Maybe not. Get paid either way.

106
00:11:40.380 --> 00:11:48.180
Your D.I.H. system: One. Per-patient subsidies: The more patients who join your trial, the more funding you get.

107
00:11:48.940 --> 00:11:57.880
Patients vote with their enrollment. Two. Variable subsidy rates: Rare diseases get higher per-patient subsidies.

108
00:11:58.720 --> 00:12:07.660
Small patient pools don't mean small budgets. Three. Results-based continuation: Deliver results, get more funding.

109
00:12:08.320 --> 00:12:15.160
Don't deliver, get defunded. Like every other job on your planet except, somehow, research.

110
00:12:16.200 --> 00:12:22.220
Pay your scientists like you pay your plumbers: for fixing the problem, not for explaining why it's hard.

111
00:12:23.400 --> 00:12:28.520
How It Works For Your Patients. Your D.I.H. doesn't replace your healthcare system.

112
00:12:29.140 --> 00:12:32.820
It adds an "experimental treatment insurance layer" on top.

113
00:12:33.440 --> 00:12:40.440
Your species already understands insurance. You just hadn't thought to apply it to not dying of untreated diseases.

114
00:12:41.680 --> 00:12:46.620
Sarah has Type two Diabetes. Old system: Metformin not working.

115
00:12:46.720 --> 00:12:51.130
No other options covered. Pays five hundred dollars per month for branded drug.

116
00:12:51.540 --> 00:12:57.920
Still has poor control. With your D.I.H.: Her doctor checks the trial network during a regular visit.

117
00:12:58.340 --> 00:13:02.560
Sees five relevant trials. Recommends one based on Sarah's profile.

118
00:13:03.140 --> 00:13:07.770
Sarah enrolls with one click. The trial coverage pool covers all costs.

119
00:13:08.100 --> 00:13:13.460
Sarah pays a thirty dollar copay. Gets an experimental drug that might work better.

120
00:13:13.460 --> 00:13:17.360
Reports blood sugar via app. Her data helps the next patient.

121
00:13:18.280 --> 00:13:25.220
Total time added to doctor visit: three minutes. Cost per patient per month: D.I.H.

122
00:13:25.280 --> 00:13:32.280
trial coverage costs three hundred and ten to two thousand five hundred and ten dollars (medication plus monitoring plus

123
00:13:32.280 --> 00:13:39.680
data collection). Traditional trials cost six thousand eight hundred to thirteen thousand six hundred dollars.

124
00:13:40.780 --> 00:13:48.920
The efficiency gain is seventy-five to eighty percent. Why your doctors will cooperate: More treatment options for desperate

125
00:13:48.920 --> 00:13:55.120
patients. C.M.E. credits for participation. No liability (covered by trial insurance).

126
00:13:55.800 --> 00:14:04.060
One click in their E.M.R. No new systems to learn. Why your patients will use it: Affordable access to experimental treatments

127
00:14:04.660 --> 00:14:10.900
(twenty to fifty dollar copay). Doctor-recommended. Insurance-like coverage (familiar model).

128
00:14:11.480 --> 00:14:15.460
No financial risk. They help others while helping themselves.

129
00:14:16.340 --> 00:14:20.840
It's like being a guinea pig, except the guinea pig gets paid and gets medicine.

130
00:14:22.080 --> 00:14:29.160
How Your Politicians Get Aligned. Your politicians optimize for reelection, status, and post-office careers.

131
00:14:29.700 --> 00:14:33.580
'Humans continuing to exist' doesn't appear on their performance review.

132
00:14:34.260 --> 00:14:37.620
This is a design flaw in your democracy, not a moral failing.

133
00:14:38.420 --> 00:14:46.160
Well, it's both. But mostly it's a design flaw, because if you put saints in a badly designed system, you get the same results.

134
00:14:46.760 --> 00:14:55.720
You just feel more betrayed. Incentive Alignment Bonds solve this by making 'support pragmatic clinical trial funding' the

135
00:14:55.720 --> 00:15:00.960
career-optimal move: Public Good Scores track voting records on health policy.

136
00:15:02.100 --> 00:15:06.240
Electoral support flows to high-scorers via independent PACs.

137
00:15:07.540 --> 00:15:13.180
Post-office opportunities (fellowships, boards) reserved for leaders who governed well.

138
00:15:13.940 --> 00:15:22.560
No bribes. No corruption. Just a standing rule: support policies that measurably reduce suffering and your political career

139
00:15:22.560 --> 00:15:27.800
gets easier. Oppose them and it gets harder. Your politicians will figure it out.

140
00:15:28.180 --> 00:15:35.520
They're not stupid. They got elected, which requires a very specific and impressive type of intelligence, none of which

141
00:15:35.520 --> 00:15:40.660
involves curing diseases. How the Money Flows. The Architecture.

142
00:15:41.380 --> 00:15:46.120
The one percent Treaty Fund: It holds the treasury (from the one percent Treaty).

143
00:15:46.640 --> 00:15:50.740
It allocates between infrastructure and public goods via Wishocracy.

144
00:15:51.580 --> 00:15:58.300
It funds campaigns, not bureaucracies. There is no C.E.O., no board, and no one to corrupt.

145
00:15:59.560 --> 00:16:06.050
Your Decentralized Institute of Health, or D.I.H.: It is a thin coordination protocol.

146
00:16:07.120 --> 00:16:15.420
It receives funding *from* the one percent Treaty Fund. Research allocation is managed via patient subsidies (market mechanism).

147
00:16:16.320 --> 00:16:27.360
It verifies results and pays for outcomes. Your D.F.D.A. (a decentralized F.D.A.): It is a funded CAMPAIGN, not part of

148
00:16:27.360 --> 00:16:32.300
your D.I.H. itself. It provides technical infrastructure for trials.

149
00:16:32.300 --> 00:16:38.120
It competes with other research models for funding. It has no budget authority (just a service provider).

150
00:16:39.660 --> 00:16:49.040
The Fund Flow. Your one percent Treaty redirects twenty-seven point two billion dollars a year from global military budgets

151
00:16:49.280 --> 00:16:56.800
into the one percent Treaty Fund. But not all of it reaches research (some of it goes to keeping the machine running): VICTORY

152
00:16:56.800 --> 00:17:03.800
Bond investors receive a ten percent share, totaling two point seven two billion dollars, to repay campaign funders.

153
00:17:05.040 --> 00:17:11.920
Political incentives (incentive alignment bonds, or I.A.B.s) receive a ten percent share, totaling two point seven two billion

154
00:17:11.920 --> 00:17:19.880
dollars, to keep politicians aligned. The research treasury receives an eighty percent share, totaling twenty-one point

155
00:17:19.880 --> 00:17:23.900
eight billion dollars, for patient subsidies (market allocation).

156
00:17:24.780 --> 00:17:33.100
What Gets Funded: Market Failures Only. Most research allocation happens automatically (patients choose trials, funding

157
00:17:33.100 --> 00:17:37.740
flows there). Your one percent Treaty Fund primarily funds MARKET FAILURES.

158
00:17:38.760 --> 00:17:41.720
These are the things your ecosystem can't handle on its own.

159
00:17:43.060 --> 00:17:47.880
Infrastructure Development and operations. Competing alternative implementations.

160
00:17:48.780 --> 00:17:54.640
Data commons infrastructure (storage, processing). Security audits and fraud detection systems.

161
00:17:55.660 --> 00:18:00.500
True Public Goods (No Revenue Model) Patient trial participation subsidies.

162
00:18:01.620 --> 00:18:07.340
Negative results publishing. Replication studies. This is minimal by design.

163
00:18:08.120 --> 00:18:15.820
Your ecosystem handles most research funding automatically: companies register treatments, patients join trials, revenue

164
00:18:15.820 --> 00:18:24.800
flows, research happens. Your decentralized institutes of health, or D.I.H., only directs the one percent Treaty Fund to

165
00:18:24.940 --> 00:18:30.160
cover what the market genuinely can't. What Your D.I.H. Outsources (and Why).

166
00:18:31.100 --> 00:18:39.260
Your D.I.H. is intentionally minimal. It outsources everything operational because the best way to avoid corruption is to

167
00:18:39.260 --> 00:18:47.100
have nothing worth corrupting: Crowdfunding is outsourced to Gitcoin, Juicebox, and others because they already exist and

168
00:18:47.100 --> 00:18:54.030
work. Task decomposition is outsourced to A.I. services because machines are better at this.

169
00:18:54.180 --> 00:18:59.120
Talent matching is outsourced to existing marketplaces so you don't reinvent LinkedIn.

170
00:18:59.920 --> 00:19:07.070
Trial infrastructure is outsourced to the D.F.D.A. (a decentralized Food and Drug Administration), which is a funded campaign,

171
00:19:07.740 --> 00:19:14.180
to separate concerns. Data storage is outsourced to competing providers to encourage market competition.

172
00:19:15.100 --> 00:19:23.290
How Campaigns Plug In. Your D.F.D.A. (a decentralized Food and Drug Administration) is the main example of a funded campaign.

173
00:19:23.840 --> 00:19:27.980
It's not part of your D.I.H. It's a service provider competing for funding.

174
00:19:28.600 --> 00:19:33.450
If it stops performing, you fund something better. This is how your species runs restaurants.

175
00:19:34.120 --> 00:19:42.780
Time to try it with medicine. Campaign Lifecycle. One. Proposal: Submit campaign description, budget, and milestones.

176
00:19:43.760 --> 00:19:48.840
Two. Wishocracy vote: Humanity decides priority relative to alternatives.

177
00:19:49.880 --> 00:19:55.280
Three. Funding: Treasury allocates based on vote plus Optimocracy recommendations.

178
00:19:56.220 --> 00:20:01.700
Four. Execution: Campaign delivers services (trials, infrastructure, and so on).

179
00:20:02.800 --> 00:20:07.540
Five. Verification: Measure outcomes against milestones. Six.

180
00:20:08.140 --> 00:20:13.940
Continuation: Results determine next year's funding. Anti-Capture Design.

181
00:20:14.800 --> 00:20:21.980
Your current system is trivially captured. Concentrate billions of dollars in a few committees, and lobbyists will find

182
00:20:21.980 --> 00:20:29.460
them. This is as predictable as gravity, and your species keeps being surprised by it the way a dog is surprised by a vacuum

183
00:20:29.460 --> 00:20:37.260
cleaner. Every single time. Your D.I.H. makes capture economically irrational.

184
00:20:37.260 --> 00:20:44.080
How Your D.I.H. Resists Capture. Mechanism: No C.E.O. How it works: Nothing to bribe.

185
00:20:44.620 --> 00:20:48.800
Capture cost: Not applicable. Mechanism: Algorithmic governance.

186
00:20:49.500 --> 00:20:54.420
How it works: Rules in smart contracts. Capture cost: Can't bribe an if-statement.

187
00:20:56.040 --> 00:21:00.180
Mechanism: Public ledger. How it works: Every dollar tracked.

188
00:21:00.900 --> 00:21:08.020
Capture cost: Corruption is visible. Mechanism: Forkable. How it works: Anyone can clone the protocol.

189
00:21:08.760 --> 00:21:13.920
Capture cost: Capture triggers replacement. Mechanism: Distributed voting.

190
00:21:14.280 --> 00:21:20.880
How it works: Millions vote via Wishocracy. Capture cost: Lobbying doesn't scale.

191
00:21:21.400 --> 00:21:26.920
Mechanism: Outcome-based funding. How it works: Results determine allocation.

